Specifically:

  `mod.rs`     is `paddlespeech/t2s/frontend/tone_sandhi.py` — the `ToneSandhi`
               class: `pre_merge_for_modify` and its six merges, and
               `modified_tone` with `_bu_sandhi`, `_yi_sandhi`,
               `_neural_sandhi` and `_three_sandhi`.

  `mod.rs`     is also `_merge_erhua` from
               `paddlespeech/t2s/frontend/zh_frontend.py`.

  `tables.rs`  is the data those two read: `must_neural_tone_words` and
               `must_not_neural_tone_words` from `tone_sandhi.py`, and
               `must_erhua` and `not_erhua` from `zh_frontend.py`.

It is a **port and not a copy**: the Python is written against `pypinyin`'s
syllables and Python jieba, and this is written against `pinyin-pro`'s readings
and `jieba-rs`. The three places it deliberately answers differently are listed
at the top of `mod.rs` beside this file, and every other
difference found by the comparison turned out to be the reader's.

